! ax4b_5i_prog_ix_x0.strap -- jb_ax4b "I-BOX 4", routine 148 (1248,
! "INDEX MODIFICATION TEST", banner PDF p.113), TEST 5I "PROG IX WITH
! IX 0", the last block of routine 148, with what follows it:
!
!   PDF p.152  011270.00-011275.40  TEST 5I and its exit
!   PDF p.152  011276.00-011305.40  routine 148's continuity update and
!                                   check (never run here: SSW halts)
!   PDF p.152  011306.00-011307.00  IC248, ICK248
!   PDF p.152  011310.00-011320.00  148S1 "SUBROUTINE TO CLEAR ALL IX
!                                   REGS." and its return 148S2
!   PDF p.153  011352.00, 011364.00 148K25, 148XW4
!
! No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited by PDF page and octal
! location.  Read from the page images at 150 and 300 dpi; checked row
! for row by tests/verify_ax4b_5i_prog_ix_x0_listing.py (48 rows, 6
! symbols).
!
! WHAT IT TESTS (IBM's code, unchanged).  After 148S1 clears every index
! register, "LX,$X0,148XW4" loads $X0 with 148K25's address (count 1).
!   L(BU),0             0.00 80 000000.20 50   I = 0, P = 0
! must load word 0 (zero): "NOT PROG IX WITH I FLD ZERO USES IX 0 TO
! GENERATE EFFECT ADR."  A nonzero result takes BZRZ,SERS, with SIC,SEN
! naming 011273.40.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points: SSW (001301.00) is a PASS halt, SERS
!     (001304.00) a FAIL halt, SEN/SENO (001310.00/001311.00) data words
!     SIC stores into.  The addresses are the listing's own (B,SSW
!     prints "1301.10 00", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SEN "1310.00 80",
!     SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80"); the contents are SSIP's, which is not
!     transcribed.  SIC "is executed if and only if the associated
!     branching is successful" (Reference Manual printed p.41, PDF 44,
!     read in the page image), so SEN stays 0 on a pass and names the
!     error entry on a failure.
!   * BIT3 and I50 (routine 150's entry) are SYN'd from the printed
!     "V+,$X12,BIT3" (13057.30 B0) and "BD,I50" (11424.04 00); both are
!     after B,SSW and never run.
!   * Notation only: the page's "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")";
!     the label glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I (I48..),
!     as for every ax4b label (docs/listing_typography.md).  Nothing
!     else changed.
!
! RESULT ON THE MODEL, 2026-11-18 (a57832f + this deck): PASSES -- halts
! at SSW (PC 1410), SEN = 0 (BZRZ not taken, so SIC,SEN stored nothing),
! $X0 = 148XW4's word (0x04BA800000040000).  CYCLES 288 is MODEL
! BEHAVIOUR; no time is printed.  IBM's listing and the model AGREE.
!
! INJECTIONS, each in a scratch copy of bsv/, OBSERVED for this deck:
!   I = 0 indexed by X0 (effAddrSigned's idx == 0 case removed) -> FAIL halt
!     (PC 1416), CYCLES 251; SEN stays 0 -- INFERRED, not dumped: SIC,SEN is
!     then itself indexed by X0 (= 148XW4's value) and stores elsewhere.
!   P = 0 treated as immediate, X0 writes dropped, FP unnormalized, FP
!     18-bit rounding, LR into J+1, SVA 19-bit: no effect on PC, SEN or
!     CYCLES (only those compared; X0RO would trip the X0 pin).
!   CONTROL: the unmodified model, the pins below (PASS, SEN = 0).
!   Each built in a scratch copy of bsv/ and restored (cmp IDENTICAL).
!
! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
! The addresses are the ones this listing prints for them (SIC,SEN
! "1310.00 80", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80", B,SSW
! "1301.10 00"), the same as routine 148's; what is AT them is SSIP's,
! which this file replaces with halts, as ax4b_148_immediate_indexed does.
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
!
! BIT3 and I50 (routine 150's entry): SYN from the printed addresses of
! "V+,$X12,BIT3" (13057.30 B0) and "BD,I50" (11424.04 00).  The rows
! after B,SSW that name them are never reached here (SSW halts first).
BIT3    SYN, (8)13057.0
I50     SYN, (8)11424.0
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.152, 011270.00-011320.00 (no printed page number on the sheet)
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)11270.0
I4848   SIC, I48S2                    ! -TEST 5I,PROG IX WITH IX 0.
        B,   I48S1
        LX,  $X0, I48XW4
        L(BU), 0
        SIC, SEN                      ! -NOT PROG IX WITH I FLD ZERO USES
        BZRZ, SERS                    ! -IX 0 TO GENERATE EFFECT ADR.
!
        B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I4848
        SIC, SENO+.32
        B,   SSW                      ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  $+.32
!
        LX,  $X13, IC248              ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY.
        SC,  $X13, $X12
        V+,  $X12, BIT3
        LC,  $X13, $X12
        SX,  $X13, IC248
!
        LX,  $X13, IC248              ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
        KV,  $X13, ICK248
        SIC, SEN
        BZXE, SERS                    ! -CONTINUITY ERROR.
        SC,  $X13, $X13
        LX,  $X12, ICK248
        SC,  $X12, $X12
        KV,  $X13, $X12
        SIC, SEN
        BZXE, SERS                    ! -CONTINUITY ERROR.
        BD,  I50
!
IC248   XW,  0, 0, 0                  ! -CONTINUITY REG 1248.
ICK248  XW,  (8)777777.77, (8)740000, 0
!
I48S1   Z,   $X0                      ! -SUBROUTINE TO CLEAR
        Z,   $X1                      ! -ALL IX REGS.
        Z,   $X3
        Z,   $X4
        Z,   $X5
        Z,   $X6
        Z,   $X7
        Z,   $X8
        Z,   $X9
        Z,   $X10
        Z,   $X11
        Z,   $X12
        Z,   $X13
        Z,   $X14
        Z,   $X15
        Z,   $X2
I48S2   $B,  0
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.153, 011352.00 and 011364.00: the constants TEST 5I reads
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)11352.0
I48K25  XW,  (8)123456.70
        SLC, (8)11364.0
I48XW4  XW,  I48K25, 1, 0
        END, I4848
